  <section>
    <h2>Behaviour in Amstelvar Avar2</h2>
    <p>
      Amstelvar Avar2 implements YTEQ through separate vertical counter-shaping
      axes for uppercase, lowercase, and figures. The transformation changes
      the vertical balance of a round counter by adjusting the vertical curve
      handles, without intentionally changing the rest of the glyph.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Uppercase round construction — O</h2>
    <p>
      O is the primary control glyph. YTEQ makes its internal counter more
      pointed or more squared in the vertical direction while the outside form
      and overall height remain stable.
    </p>

